  "rationale": "**Not satisfied: a wildcard `use = [\"*\"]` entry wakes every dormant registry plugin without naming any of them.**\n\n## How the gate works\n\n- **Which plugins are dormant.** `validate_manifest` (`src/plugins.rs`) sets `requires_use` only for `ManifestOrigin::Registry` manifests. It is set when no dependency is referenced anywhere: no `depends-on`/`depends-on(...)` (`mentions_dep`, which also counts `depends-on(*)` and ones nested in `not`/`any`/`all`) on the plugin, a skill group, a hook, an MCP server or a `[[plugins]]` edge, and no custom predicate directly in the plugin-level predicates. This matches the counting rules in `md/reference/plugin-definition.md`, which treats a plugin-level custom predicate as a gate. Subcommand gates and `SKILL.md` frontmatter do not count, so they can only make a plugin *more* dormant.\n- **What a dormant plugin needs.** `Plugin::applies` returns false when `requires_use && !ctx.is_used(&self.canonical)`, before it evaluates the plugin's predicates.\n- **Every activation path goes through `applies`.**\n  - `record_active` seeds `plugins::active_plugins` from `registry.plugins`. That active set feeds skills (`collect_skills` from `sync`), MCP servers (`sync.rs` re-checks `applies`) and hooks (`dispatch_plugin_hooks`, which also calls `applies` in `dispatched_hooks_for_payload`).\n  - `prewarm_hook_sources` and `discovery_hint` use the same active set. `prewarm_hook_sources` also re-checks `applies`.\n  - Subcommands and help go through `subcommand_dispatch::find_subcommand`. `status` calls `applies` too.\n  - Each of these builds its context with `PredicateContext::new(..).with_used(&used)`, where `used = discovery::used_plugins(..)`.\n  - When there is no workspace, the hook paths leave `used` empty, so the plugin stays dormant.\n- **What fills the used set.** `used_plugins` keeps a registry plugin only when `PluginsConfig::is_used_in` matches one of the `use` entries that apply in this workspace (`used_names_in`, scoped through `UseEntry::applies_in`) against the plugin's manifest name.\n\n## Tests (all pass, run here)\n\n- `plugins::tests::dormant_plugin_applies_only_when_used`: not applied without a used set, or with another plugin's id; applied only with its own canonical id.\n- `plugins::tests::dormancy_honors_gates_at_every_level`: which gates count toward dormancy.\n- `discovery::tests::use_wakes_a_registry_plugin_only_by_its_exact_name`: `requires_use` holds, and `my_plugin` does not wake `my-plugin`.\n- `tests/enablement.rs` `use_wakes_and_remove_sleeps_a_dormant_plugin`: no skill after a plain `sync`; installed after `use`; reaped after `use --remove`.\n- `tests/enablement.rs` `plugins_entries_match_registry_plugin_names_exactly`: `auto-enable = [\"gateless-plugin\"]` and a folded `use` spelling do not wake the plugin.\n\n## Violation\n\n`is_used_in` calls `name_matches` (`src/config.rs`), which returns true for `entry == \"*\"` regardless of the package. So `[plugins] use = [\"*\"]` puts **every** registry plugin's canonical id in `used`, and `applies` then activates every dormant plugin, although no `use` entry names it.\n\nReproduced against the prebuilt `target/debug/cargo-agents`:\n- Setup: a temp `SYMPOSIUM_HOME`, a gateless `user-plugins` entry `dormant` with a `[[skills]] source.path = \"skills\"` group, and `use = [\"*\"]`.\n- `status` reports `dormant` as active via `` `[plugins] use` ``.\n- `sync` installs its skill into `.claude/skills/dg`.\n- With `use = []`, `status` shows it as dormant.\n\n`\"*\"` is documented only for `auto-enable` (and implied for `disable`). For `use`, the reference says a dormant plugin waits \"until you enable it by name\". The same entry is also treated inconsistently: `enabled_dependencies` treats `\"*\"` as a literal crate name, and status lists it as \"not a registry plugin, a dependency or a cached crate\". The `\"*\"` case is untested.\n\n## Further notes (not counted as violations)\n\n- A dormant plugin's `[[predicate]]` definitions are registered unconditionally (`build_custom_predicate_registry`). `sync`'s `resolve_custom_predicate_entries` acquires their installations even for dormant plugins. This is documented (\"Registration is unconditional\") and does not activate the plugin's skills, hooks, MCP servers or subcommands.\n- A plugin whose only gate is a top-level custom predicate is not dormant. That follows the documented definition of \"references a dependency\".\n\n## Fix needed\n\nEither stop `name_matches` treating `\"*\"` as a wildcard for `use` entries, or document `use = [\"*\"]` and reword the requirement.\n",
  "requirement": "Symposium MUST NOT activate a registry plugin that no dependency gates unless an applicable `[plugins] use` entry names it."
}
